# Test: traffic usage ADDED over SSH to a running daemon reaches its monitor
# Initial config: a daemon with one iBGP peer and no `traffic` root, so the
#                 traffic-usage plugin is not loaded.
# Live change:    an SSH session editor load-merges `traffic usage` on the
#                 loopback interface, and commits with `commit now`.
# Expected:       `show log recent component traffic.usage` holds no attach
#                 line before the commit and holds one after it, polled so the
#                 daemon stays up until the monitor has run.
#                 The traffic-usage monitor reconciles the committed interface
#                 and tries to attach its eBPF program to it: the log carries
#                 "traffic-usage: attached" (privileged host) or
#                 "traffic-usage: attach failed" (unprivileged host), each
#                 naming interface=lo. Either line is written only by the
#                 reconcile step, for an interface in the committed config that
#                 is present and up.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-terminal-demo-showcase AC-2 (traffic usage topic) -- the
#            topic's configuration committed through the SSH editor, the path
#            the recording types, reaches the plugin's monitor on a daemon
#            started without it.
# PREVENTS: a topic recording whose commit reports success while the monitor
#           never sees the interface. It was red on exactly that until
#           rootHasChanges (internal/component/plugin/server/reload.go)
#           matched the added `traffic` key as an ancestor of the plugin's
#           root `traffic/usage`. tcp_connections=1 also proves adding
#           traffic usage leaves the BGP session alone.
#
# This proves the control plane only. Loading the eBPF program needs CAP_BPF in
# the initial user namespace, which an unprivileged host never has
# (kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled), so the counters themselves are the
# showcase lab's job in its privileged renderer container (spec A-6).
#
# PLATFORM: skipped on darwin, as ospf-added-live.ci is: the interface
# dependency has no default backend there.
option=skip-os:value=darwin
option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.log.traffic.usage:value=info

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=linger:value=true
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER

tmpfs=traffic-usage-added-live.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
    authentication {
        user admin {
            password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
        }
    }
}

environment {
    ssh {
        enabled true
        server main {
            ip 127.0.0.1;
            port $PORT2;
        }
    }
}

bgp {
    router-id 1.2.3.4
    peer peer1 {
        connection {
            remote {
                ip 127.0.0.1
            }
            local {
                ip 127.0.0.1
                accept false
            }
        }
        session {
            asn {
                local 1
                remote 1
            }
            router-id 1.2.3.4
            family {
                ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=traffic-usage-topic.conf:terminator=EOF_TOPIC
traffic {
    usage {
        enabled true
        interfaces {
            interface lo {
                track-ip true
                max-entries 256
            }
        }
        interval 250
    }
}
EOF_TOPIC

tmpfs=traffic-usage-added-live.script:terminator=EOF_SCRIPT
cli show log recent component traffic.usage
lacks traffic-usage: att
send load file absolute merge traffic-usage-topic.conf
wait Configuration merged from
send commit now
wait Session committed:
has traffic-usage: att
EOF_SCRIPT

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze start traffic-usage-added-live.conf:timeout=60s
reject=stderr:pattern=traffic-usage: interface not found
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture plugin/session-editor $PORT2 traffic-usage-added-live.conf traffic-usage-added-live.script:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=traffic-usage: (attached|attach failed).*interface=lo
